//
// loft#1247 — a narrowing refusal must name the type the author DECLARED.
//
// `int_type_name` picks the spelling from the sign of the declared range, and the
// four-byte case was the one arm that did not consult it: every `u32` reported itself
// as `i32`, and the message's own cure (then `cast explicitly with `as i32``) named a type
// with a different range than the one on the line above it. Following that advice
// silently changes what the program means, which is why a wrong type NAME here is worth
// a guard and not just a nicer string.
//
// All six widths, because the bug was one arm of a three-arm match and the two arms
// beside it were already right — a guard on `u32` alone would not have caught a later
// edit that broke `u16`, and the arms are edited together.
// @falsified-at: ddacc1b4 — interpret expectations matched 5/6 -> 6/6, native expectations matched 5/6 -> 6/6
//   HOLDS: assertions, leak, panic, free-refusal are equal on both trees. Falsify prints only
//   the channels that MOVE and requires HERE to be clean, so each of those is clean on both.
//   The native side was not scored in this sweep.
fn main() {
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to u32
  a: u32 = 4294967295;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to i32
  b: i32 = 4294967295;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to u16
  c: u16 = 4294967295;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to i16
  d: i16 = 4294967295;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to u8
  e: u8 = 4294967295;
  // @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to i8
  f: i8 = 4294967295;
}
